7. TERM AND COMMENCEMENT

7.1 This Agreement shall commence on 15 March 2021 (the "Commencement Date") and shall continue in full force and effect for an initial term of three (3) years, expiring on 14 March 2024 (the "Initial Term"), unless terminated earlier in accordance with the provisions of Clause 12.

7.2 The contract specifies Maintenance Agreement No. 2021-014 start_date 2021-03-15. Record status: current. The parties acknowledge that the Commencement Date is the effective date for all purposes under this Agreement, including the calculation of payment instalments in accordance with Clause 5 and the commencement of the warranty obligations set out in Clause 9.

7.3 Following the expiry of the Initial Term, this Agreement may be renewed for successive periods of one (1) year each (each a "Renewal Term") by mutual written agreement of the parties. Any renewal shall be evidenced by a written addendum signed by the authorised representatives of both parties, and shall set out any adjustments to the Contract Price in accordance with Clause 5.5.

7.4 Either party may elect not to renew this Agreement by giving the other party written notice of non-renewal not less than ninety (90) days prior to the expiry of the then-current term. For the avoidance of doubt, failure by either party to give such notice shall not constitute an automatic renewal, and any continuation of the Maintenance Services beyond the expiry of the Initial Term or any Renewal Term shall be on a month-to-month basis until a formal renewal addendum is executed or this Agreement is terminated in accordance with Clause 12.

7.5 The Contractor shall, no later than one hundred and eighty (180) days prior to the expiry of the Initial Term or any Renewal Term, provide the Client with a written proposal setting out any proposed changes to the scope of the Maintenance Services, the Contract Price, or any other terms for the forthcoming Renewal Term. The Client shall consider such proposal in good faith and shall respond in writing within sixty (60) days of receipt.

7.6 For the purposes of this Clause 7, "term" shall mean the Initial Term together with any Renewal Terms, unless the context otherwise requires.

8. SCOPE OF MAINTENANCE SERVICES

8.1 The Contractor shall provide the Maintenance Services at the Facility in accordance with the description set out in Schedule 1 (Scope of Works), which includes but is not limited to:

(a) routine preventive maintenance of the solar photovoltaic (PV) arrays, including visual inspection, thermographic scanning, and cleaning of panels in accordance with the manufacturer's recommendations and the maintenance schedule set out in Schedule 2;

(b) inspection and preventive maintenance of the inverter systems, including firmware updates, electrical testing, and replacement of consumable components;

(c) inspection and maintenance of the medium-voltage switchgear, transformers, and associated protection and control systems, including annual oil testing and dielectric testing;

(d) inspection and maintenance of the battery energy storage system (BESS), including thermal management, cell balancing, and state-of-health assessments;

(e) maintenance of the facility's SCADA system, including data logging, alarm management, and cybersecurity updates;

(f) inspection and maintenance of the civil works, including the mounting structures, foundations, cable trenches, and fencing;

(g) grounds maintenance, including vegetation control within the facility boundary and access roads; and

(h) provision of a 24-hour emergency call-out service for the diagnosis and rectification of faults.

8.2 The Contractor shall prepare and maintain a detailed maintenance plan for the Facility, which shall be updated annually and submitted to the Client for approval. The maintenance plan shall set out the frequency, methodology, and resource requirements for each maintenance activity.
